  "query_preview": "..\nA quiet pattern continues through Friday with little to no light\nshowers. Friday night, scattered showers and isolated thunderstorms\nwill be possible for Tinian and Saipan as Invest 99W tracks through\nthe far northern CNMI, likely between Alamagan and Agrihan. Model\nguidance shows 99W slowly strengthening, possibly moving through the\nislands as a tropical depression or weak tropical storm. However,\nGuam and Rota will likely remain dry with light winds. Breezy\nconditions appear unlikely at this time for Tinian and Saipan, and\nwould be limited to any thunderstorms. Afterwards, periods of\nisolated to low end scattered trade wind showers will likely return\nfor the rest of the forecast period.",
